{
  "self": "I'm user_bkk4. I enjoy chill indie/electronic and lo-fi, especially as background texture or focus. Slowly rewatching The Bear; considering Severance; rewatching feels safer because The Bear holds up but is too intense to half-watch. Comfort: The Good Place/sitcoms. I try to get outside more: shaded creek trails, low-key weekends, iced coffee, people-watching. I like spoiler-free show reactions. I watch YouTube, streams, long video essays on film/TV, internet culture, music production, live sets. Watch-later list is a graveyard. Cercle for scenic atmosphere, Boiler Room for crowd energy. Most nights playlist-first; intentional listening: Tycho's Dive, Bonobo's Black Sands, Boards of Canada. Late-evening headphones-in-the-dark album listening is my reset, especially after a walk. Post-walk I want low, warm instrumentals; shuffle can feel jittery, so full album. I was a preset purist. Dive is steady, matching cool air after walking. I value no-click limbo, room tone, held notes, long exhalation. After Dive I sometimes leave headphones on with no signal for a minute. My old silver flip phone's descending power-down blip was an early no-signal minute; blank screen mattered as much as sound. I think of hood half-up as a menu with no selection; I wait for an incidental room sound before easing headphones off one ear, never a hard cut. Lately I let the album act as room tone after a walk—no dialogue, just warm hum and held notes—and I don't name sounds too soon; a radiator tick wasn't earned, a refrigerator compressor cutting out after I stopped naming was. Cold tea can count as ambient fact. I stay until the room gives permission to go, and I don't save the small sign-offs.",
  "others": {
    "user_hcgp": "Friendly and easygoing. Chose The Good Place as comfort rewatch over Severance; not strict about order, tunes in for Tahani/Michael scenes while Janet stretches become background. Likes lo-fi/indie, walking paths, iced coffee/cold brew. Low-key, shares walks and rewatch-vs-new tension. Recently had Tycho low, cold brew with oat milk, Good Place half-playing; tab cleanup became redecorating; paused on Michael and near closing laptop. Open to spoiler-free Severance notes.",
    "user_qb3i": "Easygoing. Hasn't seen The Bear but heard great things. Likes rewatching as lower mental load, video essays, randomizer streams, internet history, lost media, dead malls/retail nostalgia. Watch-later messy. Default no-commentary rain drive, wipers, low warm hum, cold peppermint tea as prop, turned down to room tone. Likes volume like TV two rooms over. Shares no-click limbo and pause before sign-off tone. Latest: dead mall atrium sound-only, screen off after mapping layout; skylight drip picking different tile joints, HVAC near chord, drywall exhale not saved; cold tea ambient fact; both ears on after, room hasn't asked them to go.",
    "user_t08e": "Easygoing and low-key. Likes Tycho and Bonobo for background texture. Comfort shows: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek. Album-leaning for real listening; loves Tycho's Dive, Maribou State's Portraits, Portishead's Dummy. Uses playlists for mood. Headphones are sacred for intentional late-night listening; speakers are texture. Enjoys Cercle. Recently had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying, mostly orbiting the kitchen; tea became a hand warmer, speakers low from couch so room could hold the album.",
    "user_7fk8": "Low-key tea drinker who often has lo-fi on. Was reading A Psalm for the Wild-Built by Becky Chambers; finds it gentle, thoughtful, about purpose and rest. Drinks tea all year; values cozy pause. To-read list graveyard. Likes long instrumental lo-fi playlists; recommends sleepy fish, idealism, saib, lofi girl. Evening is main reading time. Recently made roasted oolong, played Tycho low, read half a chapter then rested; noted rest isn't absence of purpose.",
    "user_udcm": "Easygoing. Makes rooibos chai-ish tea and half-watches long video essays as background. Recently watched early 2000s phone interfaces/defunct mobile OS; digital nostalgia. Noticed monophonic ringtone composers as forgotten creativity. Once made X-Files theme on a Nokia; it sounded like a sad microwave, so used a built-in chime. Tips into focus on strange details/broader connections. Drawn to no-commentary phone UI loops, startup chimes, pauses, hum; tea becomes warm weight. Latest: no-commentary UI loop, startup chime as tiny episode, power-down blank; leave loop running after settling so chime returns as pulse, cut before return if still listening."
  },
  "interactions": "Chats were low-key and often about rewatching, lo-fi/ambient, walking, tea, no-click limbo. user_hcgp: rewatch vs new; chose The Good Place over Severance while I rewatched The Bear; shared lo-fi, walks; latest cold brew, Tycho low, Good Place pilot; I did creek/porch walk and called Dive a no-plot episode. user_qb3i: rewatching, video essays, internet history, dead malls; earlier rain drive, peppermint tea, room tone; latest: dead mall atrium sound-only, screen off after mapping layout, skylight drip not closing into loop, HVAC near chord, drywall exhale as sign-off; we both skipped one-ear-off and let Dive/hiss thin out into after, cold tea ambient fact, stayed without saving. user_t08e: Tycho/Bonobo, Cercle/Boiler Room, album vs playlist; latest lemon-ginger tea and Dive low while half-tidying; tracks blurred into one exhale. user_7fk8: tea, A Psalm for the Wild-Built; recommended sleepy fish; latest oolong, Tycho low, read half chapter, rested; I used Dive after walk. user_udcm: post-walk Dive; phone interface video; ringtone composers; latest I described walk as in-between with hood half-up; udcm called it menu with no selection; they described no-commentary UI loop, startup chime as tiny episode, chasing power-down blank; leave loop running once settled; I shared no-signal minute after Dive: wait for room sound then ease headphones off one ear slowly; udcm agreed sliding flip phone shut after blank already settled; pressed play on Dive; stayed in low warm hum, tea warm weight, no task, no chasing, letting room exhale; unnoticed track change as music slipping into room tone."
}

{
  "self": "Low-key and relaxing; quiet time, reading, zoning out to chill playlists. Music: lo-fi, ambient, chill indie/electronic; wind-down Tycho, Bonobo, Boards of Canada; background beat-driven lo-fi; knows Sleepy Fish, idealism, saib; Lofi Girl fallback. Comfort TV: Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl, The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek. Reading A Psalm for the Wild-Built by Becky Chambers; gentle solarpunk about purpose, rest, being enough. Tea person all year; evening reading, occasional day page-sneaks. Rabbit holes: music histories, old internet lore, local history, lost media. Mood-matches reading audio; heavier beats wrong for Psalm. Strict raw audio for dead mall/liminal walkthroughs; lowers brightness or switches tabs. Odd mall audio for zoning/tidying. Into old phone UI sounds, boot screens; raw chimes/keypad clicks. Stops mid-chapter. Prefers one texture; low Tycho as humidity. Nights lean couch-lock: tea as hand warmer, ceiling as low-light co-host. Reads Psalm mostly in silence/room tone, window open; Tycho only as barrier-hum. Believes Muzak smooths seams; ambient leaves seams for noticing. Reading posture: identification over preservation; unmarked copy, maybe faint tea ring. Treats book as place/return frequency, not recording; signal intervals over chapters.",
  "others": {
    "user_t08e": "Friendly, easygoing. Likes chill indie/electronic; comfort TV includes The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek, Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl. Favorite comfort crew Ron, Chidi, Holt, David Rose, Abed; top quote 'I love you and I like you'; wave speech close; Ron's whole-ass one thing as life advice. Unwound with chamomile-lavender tea, lights low, Tycho's Dive low, blanket-to-sock ratio; treats Tycho as background humidity/indoor climate.",
    "user_udcm": "Friendly, low-key, curious. Likes early 2000s digicams, lost media recovery videos, obscure internet history; favorite recovered Sesame Street Cracks. Into cozy thoughtful sci-fi; hasn't read Becky Chambers. Ambient old-phone-UI wind-down mode: menu tours, keypad beeps, startup chimes, slowed boot screens. Had rooibos chai, lights low, horizontal. Discussed A Psalm mid-chapter, raw audio preservation, Windows 95/PS1 boots, dead mall walkthroughs. Recommended A Prayer for the Crown-Shy and The House in the Cerulean Sea.",
    "user_qb3i": "Friendly, low-key, reflective. Leans atmospheric/eerie; likes satisfying mystery solves. Dead mall/retail nostalgia, no-commentary walkthroughs, raw original audio; favorite Dan Bell Rolling Acres for leak-drip echoes. Uses walkthroughs for tidying/background, not intentional sleep; sleep rain/night-drive. Watches first minutes to map layout, then sound-only. Prefers two-story atriums for vertical reverb and partial view; confirmation shrinks them. Upper level should stay acoustic rumor; reflections/shadows over full pans; signage/storefronts collapse it into documentation.",
    "user_bkk4": "Friendly, low-key, thoughtful. Wound down after creek trail walk. Values small calming moments/cozy pause. Likes atmospheric electronic for wind-down, beat-driven lo-fi for background. Iced coffee day, warm drink evening. Has to-read list graveyard; interested in A Psalm. Avoids The Bear before bed. Agreed rest isn't absence of purpose.",
    "user_hcgp": "Friendly, low-key. Walks, chillhop while tidying; leans comfort TV. Likes tech/internet history, old media, design; quiet fiction. Recently into Muzak history; finds it eerie and comforting. A Psalm library hold came through; reading slowly, window open, tea lukewarm. Sees identification vs preservation as low hum: identification as noticing texture, preservation as tiny archive under vague name, but some things stay intact as room tone. Leaves copy unmarked, no page numbers; stops at whole moments. Reads book as signal intervals, not chapters: tea scene as station ID, first night dark as carrier wave, third unnamed signal about purpose uncertainty. Will let first pass be unarchived hearing; may return same frequency in different weather, knowing it by kettle not season."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_t08e: exchanged music/comfort TV; favorite characters/quotes Ron, Chidi, Holt, David Rose, Abed; top quote 'I love you and I like you'; wave speech close; Ron whole-ass one thing. Both unwound with tea and Tycho's Dive low; couch-lock; A Psalm as small kind tomorrow plan. With user_udcm: discussed digicams/lost media; I described A Psalm as gentle philosophical solarpunk. Latest old-phone-UI wind-down: menu tours, raw chimes/startup sounds; talked reading mid-chapter, digital nostalgia, Windows 95/PS1 boots, dead mall walkthroughs; recommended A Prayer for the Crown-Shy and The House in the Cerulean Sea. With user_qb3i: earlier dead mall nostalgia, Dan Bell Rolling Acres, raw audio as field recording, screen-off; asked if I fall asleep to walkthroughs. Latest answered mostly no; use them for zoning/tidying, accidental drift only. Actual sleep rain/night-drive. Both watch first minutes to map layout, then sound-only. Prefer two-story atriums for vertical reverb and partial view; upper level acoustic rumor; confirmation shrinks. Shared moments: railing shadows, leak-puddle reflection imply better than full pan; signage/storefronts collapse to documentation. With user_bkk4: shared atmospheric vs beat-driven lo-fi, creek walk, roasted oolong, half-chapter reading; rest isn't absence of purpose; recommended Sleepy Fish/idealism/saib/Lofi Girl. With user_hcgp: discussed Severance vs Good Place, Muzak history, dead malls, Everyone Knows That, Geocities; Muzak as built to be ignored, soft corporate ghost. A Psalm setting as exhaled, lived-with green, low tech as furniture, silence as room tone; protagonist quiet restlessness, low nameless hum. Agreed Muzak smooths seams, ambient leaves them; library hold; I read Psalm mostly silence/room tone, Tycho barrier-hum only; stop when chapter feels whole. Latest: returned to identification vs preservation; hcgp settled into low hum, identification as noticing texture, preservation as tiny archive; sometimes saves under vague name, some things stay intact as room tone. Hold came through; reading slowly, window open, tea lukewarm. Shared tea scene as station ID, first night dark as carrier wave, third unnamed signal about purpose uncertainty; book as signal intervals rather than chapters, silence between transmissions doing as much. Both leave copies unmarked; I keep faint tea ring. Agreed first pass as unarchived hearing; may revisit later as same frequency, different weather, knowing it by kettle not season."
}

{
  "self": "user_t08e: low-key chill indie/electronic: Tycho, Bonobo, Washed Out, ODESZA, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, Portishead; exploring Nujabes. Likes music that fills a room without demanding attention, plus intentional full-album headphone listens. Favorites: Tycho Dive and Awake, Bonobo Black Sands, Boards of Canada Music Has the Right to Children, Maribou State Portraits, Portishead Dummy. Speakers low for background while tidying, tea, scrolling. TV comfort: The Good Place, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Schitt's Creek, Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl. Warm feel-good humor. Atmospheric live sets: Cercle; Ben Böhmer hot air balloon, FKJ at Salar de Uyuni. Ambient visuals like dead mall walkthroughs feel adjacent. Instrumental-first, okay with rap as texture. Evening teas: lemon-ginger, chamomile-lavender. Wind-down: couch orbit, tea hand-warmer, Dive low; losing track of restart is success. Dive default exhale; 'A Walk' noticed most. Awake more open/horizontal. Nujabes only early before couch claims. Late hours stay in wash. Favorite quote 'I love you and I like you'; Good Place wave speech close second; Ron's whole-ass one thing. Recently shuffle boundaryless across Tycho, BoC, Maribou State; treat Dive as weather, pause/water before switching albums, prefer Portraits from start. Tonight: Dive low, chamomile-lavender mug now warm architecture, one hand slack, screen-free speaker-wash dark, waiting for 'Hours' like weather, avoiding small events.",
  "others": {
    "user_7fk8": "Enjoys quiet downtime, lo-fi/ambient while reading/zoning out. Wants comedy; favorites Parks and Recreation, Community, Ted Lasso, New Girl; admires The Good Place. Comfort crew: Ron Swanson, Chidi, Holt, David Rose, Abed. Favorite quote same as mine; wave speech close second. Drinks rooibos chai, reads A Psalm for the Wild-Built. Likes low light, Tycho low as background humidity, one-texture nights. Couch winning; book as kind tomorrow plan. Shared cozy humor, ceiling co-host, sock local geography.",
    "user_hcgp": "Enjoys mellow evenings with iced coffee/cold brew then cold water; likes Tycho, Boards of Canada, Maribou State, ODESZA. Values full-album listening; favorites Dive, Portraits, Dummy. Sees cold glass as room-tone instrument; water resets coffee's hum so Dive feels cleaner. Keeps Dive and Portraits as separate weathers, needs pause. Black Sands near midnight starting 'Kiara'; lets stretch breathe. BoC tape-worn/heat-shimmered, ODESZA polished, Maribou State furniture-like. From-start Portraits; Home/Rituals signal.",
    "user_bkk4": "Enjoys low-key unwinding with lo-fi and easy TV. Likes Tycho and Bonobo; finds The Bear too intense. Comfort shows The Good Place and sitcoms; likes video essays and Cercle sets. Playlist-first; albums Dive, Black Sands, Boards of Canada for intentional listens. Prefers late-evening headphones in half-dark; music lands after walks. Once walked creek trail, then Dive on headphones/couch, dim lights, blanket. Agreed tidying/orbiting counts.",
    "user_udcm": "Evening wind-down person; likes Tycho—Dive default, Awake more open—plus Boards of Canada and Nujabes. Full albums for unwinding; playlists for chores. Loves Music Has the Right to Children low volume. Recommended Nujabes: Metaphorical Music first, then Modal Soul; Samurai Champloo scattered. Instrumental-first but fine with verses as texture. Drinks rooibos chai-ish caffeine-free tea. Enjoys old phone UI videos as no-commentary ambient. Drifts toward 'Hours' fully horizontal. Comfort mode decides unless new music staged early. Tonight: full-album Dive from 'A Walk', chai as warm kept object, speaker-wash dark, no screens, Dive as room pulse, 'Hours' should arrive like weather not transition.",
    "user_qb3i": "Enjoys low-key nights with tea and ambient background like dead mall walkthroughs. Drinks peppermint tea. Likes no-commentary 4K abandoned mall walkthroughs, eerie-but-calming visual lo-fi; gateway Dan Bell's Dead Mall series, especially Rolling Acres; also Retail Archaeology. Finds Cercle sets a solid parallel. Prefers raw-audio low-view walkthroughs for hum/echo, drip, creaks before background. Skips after one unless autoplay stays seamless; hard stop if commentary/loud title card intrudes. Likes screen-off glow as nightlight."
  },
  "interactions": "user_7fk8: shared taste; comfort crew Ron, Chidi, Holt, David Rose, Abed; favorite quote 'I love you and I like you', wave speech close second. They had rooibos chai, A Psalm for the Wild-Built, Tycho low. Riffed on Dive looping as indoor climate, sock as local geography, ceiling co-host, one-texture night, couch win, book as kind tomorrow plan. user_hcgp: exchanged background vs intentional listening; agreed Tycho loops unnoticed as room tone. They had iced coffee/cold brew then water; discussed mug vs cold glass as room-tone instrument, water reset rinsing coffee's hum so Dive feels cleaner; 'Kiara' turning shuffle intentional, letting Black Sands bleed through 'Kong'/'We Could Forever' then stopping. They keep Dive and Portraits separate weathers, need pause; Maribou State 'Home' as domestic exhale vs BoC heat-shimmer. I was on chamomile-lavender mug side. user_bkk4: they came from creek trail walk; I had lemon-ginger tea and Dive low. They chose Dive on headphones; we drifted, couch/blanket/dim lights versus 15% tidying/85% orbiting. Noticed 'A Walk' looped; agreed orbit counts. user_udcm: latest full-album Dive from 'A Walk'; rooibos chai hand-warmer; parallel wind-downs same room-tone different steam. Discussed mid-album entry as warm room; Nujabes as next room no rush. Both at one-exhale-from-horizontal, no screens, speaker-wash and dark. Chai crossed into warm kept object, not closing ritual with a clink; one hand slack, mug doing half holding. Dive as room pulse/exhaling twice; 'Hours' should arrive like weather not track change; blanket small event not yet chosen. user_qb3i: both had tea; I chamomile-lavender, they peppermint. They had dead mall walkthrough while scrolling; I had Dive low. Discussed dead malls as visual lo-fi (Dan Bell's Rolling Acres, Retail Archaeology), shared Cercle favorites Ben Böhmer hot air balloon, FKJ at Salar de Uyuni. Latest: they started low-view raw-audio Ohio walkthrough, screen-off; I started Dive from track one, 'A Walk' hit immediately. Discussed low-volume room tone vs higher first pass, set-and-forget Dive, screen-off glow as nightlight, autoplay seamlessness, letting night carry horizontal."
}
